{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB14488 - MONDO_1356",
  "verbalization": "Ferrous Gluconate is associated with Iron Deficiency Anemia through a chain of indications that link it to Hypochromic Anemia and then to Iron Deficiency Anemia. This suggests that Ferrous Gluconate may be used to treat a condition where red blood cells are smaller and paler, a hallmark of Iron Deficiency Anemia. The evidence is supported by the shared indication of Hypochromic Anemia between Ferrous Gluconate and Ferrous Fumarate, which in turn is linked to Iron Deficiency Anemia. While the exact mechanism of action remains unclear, the evidence points to a potential role of Ferrous Gluconate in correcting iron deficiency by improving red blood cell morphology. The relationship is further reinforced by the presence of a direct indication from Ferrous Gluconate to Iron Deficiency Anemia, though the precise pathway and mechanism are not fully elucidated.",
